>>
Rule 1 (input must have a numeric dtype: integer, floating, or complex)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 2 (boolean dtype is not supported)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 3 (value ranges consistent with integer dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 1 then min(v_1) ≥ -128 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 127 else if dtype_(v_1) = 2 then min(v_1) ≥ -32768 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 32767 else if dtype_(v_1) = 3 then min(v_1) ≥ -2147483648 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 2147483647 else if dtype_(v_1) = 5 then min(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 255
>>
Rule 4 (each dimension length must be non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (supported numeric dtype set expressed by ranges)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) ∨ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∨ (9 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10)
